# LIBRARY: own
# 200 calls teach the site the one shape. Then a row gets a getter that writes the next row, another row becomes a Proxy, a third null. Each is "no" at the site: the turn begins again in the closed copy:
# the getter runs once, what it stores is seen by the next turn, the Proxy's trap sees one read, and null throws behind both.
# RUN(TWICE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# TWICE-LABEL: code f1:Body
# TWICE: = GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent {{*}}key="price"
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 241
# CHECK-NEXT: getter,proxy price
# CHECK-NEXT: TypeError
# CHECK-NEXT: getter,proxy price,getter,proxy price
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
